Today is Thursday and it is five o'clock.
I step out of the office.
This week we have started a new project.
I have finished my work early today.
My badminton game is at half past five.
I go straight to the local sports club.
I do not have my own racket.
I say to the dada at the counter, "Dada, please give me a racket on rent."
He gives me a racket and says, "Take this, Madam."
I go inside to the court.
Amit and Neha have already arrived there.
Amit is a manager in a bank and Neha is a teacher at a school.
Neha says to me, "Maya, you look very tired today!"
I smile and say, "Yes, there was a lot of work stress today."
But now I am ready to play.
We start our badminton game.
After an hour, our game finishes.
We have played very fast and well.
Now all my stress has gone away.
I return the racket to dada at the counter while leaving.
I am feeling very fresh now.
